WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.638
Imagine a Saturday job in a café. You are paid six pounds for every hour you work. Work four hours, and you earn twenty-four pounds. These are example figures.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:26.314
A wage is the payment to labour for work, often set per hour. A minimum wage is the lowest hourly pay an employer may legally pay. Gross income is pay before any tax is taken off.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:34.710
So gross income equals the hourly wage times the hours worked. Each hour adds another six pounds: six, twelve, eighteen, twenty-four.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:45.379
Step one. Find the hourly wage. Then find the hours worked in the period the question asks about, a week or a month.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:58.313
Step two. Multiply, and write the calculation down. For example, six pounds forty an hour for twenty hours. Six pounds forty times twenty is one hundred and twenty-eight pounds.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:10.637
Step three. Give the answer with the currency sign and two decimal places. Twenty hours earn far more than one hour, so a sensible answer is much bigger than the rate.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:31.370
Here is a real question from January 2020. Andorra's minimum wage rose to five euros eighty-seven per hour. Calculate the monthly gross income of a worker paid the minimum wage for one hundred and seventy-five hours a month. Two marks.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:39.041
Pick out the two figures. The hourly wage is five euros eighty-seven. The hours are one hundred and seventy-five a month.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:51.063
Five euros eighty-seven times one hundred and seventy-five is one thousand and twenty-seven euros twenty-five. That is the monthly gross income. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:02:02.059
Check it quickly. About six euros times one hundred and seventy-five is one thousand and fifty euros. Our answer is close, so there is no decimal slip.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:12.667
A common mistake is giving just the hourly rate. The question asks for a month's pay, so multiply by the hours.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:20.354
Another is a decimal slip, or leaving out the currency sign. Estimate first, and write the euro sign.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:38.879
Now you try. In an example country, a café worker is paid the minimum wage of seven pounds forty-five an hour, and works thirty-two hours a week. Calculate the weekly gross income. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.523
Seven pounds forty-five times thirty-two is two hundred and thirty-eight pounds forty.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:58.237
See how it builds. Ten hours earn seventy-four pounds fifty. Thirty hours earn two hundred and twenty-three pounds fifty. Thirty-two hours earn two hundred and thirty-eight pounds forty.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:07.046
Remember: find the rate and the hours, multiply and show it, then give the currency and two decimal places. Now try the practice questions.
